> Looking at the logic here, I feel this condition is incorrect. This will remove the \ufeff character from a file that ONLY had 1 at the beginning.

No, as I mentioned in the comment, VS Code's `applyEdit` might implicitly handle the BOM. This means VS Code is aware of the original file encoding and preserves the BOM if the file is UTF-8 with BOM. Therefore, when using `vscode.workspace.applyEdit(edit)`, the edit is expected to contain no BOM in the input.


> This also is a pragmatic fix to an agentic problem. While this will correct the output, we should try to fix the underlying problem with what is causing the model to provide this in the first place.

